clang: add x86_64-igos-linux-gnu to the GCC-installation candidate triples

clang discovers the host GCC installation (libstdc++ headers, libgcc.a,
crt objects, the gcc private libdir) by scanning /usr/lib/gcc/<triple>/
against a hardcoded per-arch alias list in the driver. This distro's
vendor triple is not upstream, so detection came up empty: the freshly
built clang++ could not find <new> (libstdc++ headers) and clang+lld
could not resolve the -lgcc member of the libgcc_s.so linker script.
Same class of entry as the redhat/suse/slackware/amazon aliases already
in the list. Proven against the built driver: without this, -v prints
no "Selected GCC installation"; with --gcc-install-dir pointed at the
same directory this patch makes discoverable, compile+link of C++
succeeds end to end.

--- a/clang/lib/Driver/ToolChains/Gnu.cpp
+++ b/clang/lib/Driver/ToolChains/Gnu.cpp
@@ -2405,7 +2405,8 @@
       "x86_64-pc-linux-gnu",    "x86_64-redhat-linux6E",
       "x86_64-redhat-linux",    "x86_64-suse-linux",
       "x86_64-manbo-linux-gnu", "x86_64-slackware-linux",
-      "x86_64-unknown-linux",   "x86_64-amazon-linux"};
+      "x86_64-unknown-linux",   "x86_64-amazon-linux",
+      "x86_64-igos-linux-gnu"};
   static const char *const X32Triples[] = {"x86_64-linux-gnux32",
                                            "x86_64-pc-linux-gnux32"};
   static const char *const X32LibDirs[] = {"/libx32", "/lib"};
